            <ArticleTitle>Ischiofemoral impingement: hip pain of infrequent cause.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>186-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.reuma.2012.06.005</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S1699-258X(12)00176-3</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Hip pain is a frequent cause of medical attention in the daily clinical practice. Among the different causes included in the differential diagnosis we find ischiofemoral impingement, described initially in patients after joint replacement surgery, but later found in patients with no history of a causal disease.</AbstractText>
